      "writtenOn": "2021-01-07T00:01:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you clarify which portion of this is a \"should\" in the compatibility spec? \n\nIs your SSD non-PD or PD for the example?  We\u0027ll bump non-PD in favor of the phone, but not bump it if the SSD is running PD and requested 3 A. \n\nAs it is, once a sink PD port has 3 A allocated, it keeps it until disconnect.  No new PD sink ports can bump it from its level.  The lowest number port criteria is used when that sink is disconnected and we now have 3 A to give someone (or if we end up balancing ports with two new 3 A sinks added near-simultaneously).",
      "parentUuid": "5a071cba_051052cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "84c22a360e1f744b9df681e76badfe864d136795",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
