      "writtenOn": "2021-01-07T00:01:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t found that from my dongle and dock pile so far.  I have several hubs which request very little (500 mA or 100 mA), and several that ask for slightly more (2.4 A), and only one which asks for all of it (3.0 A).  My sampling doesn\u0027t reflect all of the dongles in the ecosystem, I\u0027m sure, but it seems to indicate that a fair number set a reasonable operational current.\n\nI can check out the mismatch bit as well, but so far the sink capability method isn\u0027t overly greedy in my testing at least.  Let me know if your partner sampling is different.",
